      "message": "\u003e Patch Set 2:\n\u003e \n\u003e Sorry to jump in, but is this made so that OEMs can override the zram implementation with their own?\n\nYes this is to allow vendor override. Some vendors have a lot of zram customizations. We will enforce that a compatible implementation is provide with VTS tests.\n\n\u003e I\u0027ve worked on quite a lot of devices and didn\u0027t really see much /changes/ there worth moving this to vendor, and definitely something that can be done with vendor_hooks of really needed\n\u003e \n\u003e I can see this module being almost always enabled so is there really any benefit in having it a module?\n\nThe plan is to have a core zram in GKI with hooks but for the Android S time line we are allowing vendors to provide their own.\n\n",
